Connectors publish apps running on your machine through the qURL platform.

A Connector serves one local app under its ID — the route name your app
serves under. Callers never reach your machine directly: the platform
verifies each caller and grants access before any request is forwarded
to your app.

Usage:
  qurl connector [flags]
  qurl connector [command]

Examples:
  qurl connector run --id billing --target :8080

Available Commands:
  run         Serve a local app through the qURL platform

Flags:
  -h, --help   help for connector

Global Flags:
      --color string      colorize output: auto, always, or never (default auto)
      --endpoint string   qURL API endpoint (default https://api.layerv.ai)
  -o, --output string     output format: text or json (default text)
      --profile string    configuration profile name
  -q, --quiet             print only the primary value, one per line
  -v, --verbose           print request diagnostics on stderr

Use "qurl connector [command] --help" for more information about a command.
